OL,3,GNEWSAMigrants using longer, more
OL,4,Adangerous routes across Channel
OL,5,
OL,6,FA growing number of migrants are trying
OL,7,Fto cross the Channel on small boats
OL,8,Fusing longer routes from beaches
OL,9,Ffurther south and west of Calais and
OL,10,FDunkirk, French authorities say.
OL,12,FLast week one boat set off from
OL,13,FNormandy and spent more than 30 hours
OL,14,Fat sea, before being intercepted and
OL,15,Ftaken to Dover by Border Force.
OL,17,FAlthough attempts from Normandy have
OL,18,Fbeen rare, authorities in neighbouring
OL,19,FSeine-Maritime say there have already
OL,20,Fbeen 58 attempts this year, up from 30
OL,21,Flast year.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
